<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-321] CacheWriter methods should throw CacheWriterException</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-321</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Tests where CacheWriter&apos;s methods write(All)/delete(All) throw an exception expect that Cache&apos;s methods put(All)/remove(All) throw CacheWriterException in this case.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;List of tests which expect CacheWriterException if CacheWriter throws an exception:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;CacheWriterTest.shouldNotPutWhenWriteThroughFails
CacheWriterTest.shouldWriteThoughUsingPutAll_partialSuccess
CacheWriterTest.shouldNotRemoveWhenWriteThroughFails
CacheWriterTest.shouldWriteThroughRemoveAll_partialSuccess
CacheWriterTest.shouldWriteThroughRemoveAllSpecific_partialSuccess
CacheWriterTest.shouldWrapWriterExceptions
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We should make sure that these tests pass by catching IgniteException, calling hasCause(CacheWriterException.class), and if true, then throwing the CacheWriterException.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
